    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1094-a2">

                <pb facs="1172" n="1076" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1076"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.]</seg></opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hitchcock to Count
                            Lamsdorff.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-02-06"><hi rendition="#italic">February 6/18,
                            1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Your Excellency</hi>: I am profoundly touched by the
                    kind words of sympathy conveyed in your note of yesterday in referring to the
                    sad accident to the American cruiser <hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi>, by
                    which the families of so many of our brave seamen are plunged into mourning.</p>
                <pb facs="1173" n="1077" xml:id="pg1077"/>
                <p>May I beg of your excellency to convey to His Excellency Count Mouravieff, with
                    sentiments of my deep solicitude for his health, which I am gratified to learn
                    is improving, my sincere thanks for his kind and thoughtful sympathy.</p>
                <p>I avail myself, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ethan A. Hitchcock.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
